WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:13.140
Kuwait is, along with Qatar, the only country
in the Arabian Peninsula where elections are

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:15.370
held. Yep, you heard that right...

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:19.590
Many of you might know this country because
of their oil reserves, their wealth, or the

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:25.510
fact that they were invaded by SADDAM HUSSEIN
in the 90s. But Kuwait is much more than that.

00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:31.230
It is one of the most tolerant nations in
the Islamic world. Women can vote, run for

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:40.290
office, and they even have a female MP. But
not only that, &nbsp;for decades, the Kuwaiti

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:45.690
Royal House has been America’s best friend
in the Gulf. This is why, when they were invaded

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:57.140
in 1990, Uncle Sam didn’t hesitate for a
moment, and sent their troops in immediately.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:02.420
And now you might wonder: why are we talking
today about Kuwait? Well, this is the only

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:10.750
Arab country, alongside with Oman, that hasn’t
joined the diplomatic block of Qatar.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:16.250
Saudi Arabia, Bahrain, Egypt and the United
Arab Emirates&nbsp;broke off relations with Qatar&nbsp;in

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:21.570
the worst diplomatic crisis to hit Gulf Arab
states in decades. The three Gulf countries

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:26.560
and Egypt accused Qatar of supporting terrorism
and destabilizing the region.]

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:31.290
And now the question is why is Kuwait not
on this list of nations who have cut ties

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:36.240
with Qatar? What kind of interest does this
country have in this diplomatic crisis? How

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:40.530
does their political system work? Well, today,
we are going to answer these questions. But

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:46.140
before we do, let’s get to know more about
this particular part of the planet.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:49.570
WHO IS WHO IN THE PERSIAN GULF?

00:01:49.570 --> 00:01:54.410
The first country we need to know about in
the Arabian Peninsula is Saudi Arabia. Saudi

00:01:54.410 --> 00:02:00.369
Arabia is the biggest country in the region,
both in terms of population and territory.

00:02:00.369 --> 00:02:08.700
But it is not the only one... Here we have
the United Arab Emirates, which Dubai and

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:14.180
Abu Dhabi are part of. This country has its
own government, its own laws, and its own

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:17.750
currency. Is absolutely independent from the
Saudis.

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:22.100
The same goes for Qatar, which has its own
foreign policy and holds better relations

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:28.900
with public enemies of the Saudis like the
Islamic Republic of IRAN. And now you might

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:33.430
be thinking that all of this countries have
one important thing in common... the fact

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:36.360
that they are incredibly oil-rich, right?

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:41.200
Well… actually that’s pretty wrong. Here
we have the Republic of Yemen: a country that

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:50.069
is extremely poor. Now, of course, all of
this countries have a common history, traditions

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:55.050
and religion. But make no mistake, each of
them have their own peculiarities.

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:59.660
For example, the United Arab Emirates was
the first country who realized oil is not

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:05.150
forever and therefore, they decided to diversify
their economy. Today, crude represents just

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:10.120
3% of the total economy of Dubai.

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:14.850
Kuwait is also a totally different animal.
Yes, they have a monarchy, the so-called EMIR,

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:23.030
but he is controlled by a constitution and
a parliament. But hold on just a second, because

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:28.349
this doesn't mean they are a 100% democratic
country. In fact, their system is way more

00:03:28.349 --> 00:03:38.989
complicated than that. So, let’s have a
look at it.

00:03:38.989 --> 00:03:41.470
HOW DOES SEMI-DEMOCRACY WORK IN KUWAIT?

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:46.799
So, Kuwait is known as a “semi-democracy.”
Unlike Saudi Arabia, Kuwait has freedom of

00:03:46.799 --> 00:03:55.530
religion. This is why you can find even a
Catholic church in the middle of Kuwait city.

00:03:55.530 --> 00:04:00.250
Things like the HIJAB are not mandatory, and
even the laws regarding alcohol are fairly

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:04.860
liberal in comparison with it’s neighbours.
Of course, it’s still forbidden to buy it

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:08.220
or sell it. But it’s legal to drink in private.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:12.840
Nonetheless, the main peculiarity about Kuwait
are their elections. All the adult, natural-born

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:16.640
citizens have the right to vote for their
parliament every four years. This includes

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:22.390
women. In this elections, political parties
are forbidden. But this doesn't mean candidates

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:26.590
have no ideology at all. They can also campaign
freely and have debates.

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:31.100
Needless to say, the political debate here
is totally different compared to that in the

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:36.020
UK or US, for example. Here, the political
spectrum is not only a right-wing / left-wing

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:39.720
kind of thing. Of course, some candidates
are highly conservative and others are more

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:47.050
liberal and open to Western culture, but this
not the only thing that divides the Kuwaiti

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:48.050
society.

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:52.620
There is also a never-ending fight between
Sunni muslims and Shia ones. This is because,

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:57.479
as I said before, there is freedom of religion,
and that means the creed of the candidate

00:04:57.479 --> 00:05:03.479
is as important as his tax plan. But not only
that, there is another big divide between

00:05:03.479 --> 00:05:09.530
the so-called urban voters and the tribal
ones. Just think about it, this is a country

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:15.120
with a long nomadic tradition, with half of
the population still living in tribes. And

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:20.729
these tribes hold their own primaries to choose
their candidates.

00:05:20.729 --> 00:05:30.110
This said, elections are used to choose a
national assembly with the power to make laws

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:34.680
and even put a veto on the policies taken
by the executive branch.

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:38.290
And now you might be wondering… How do they
choose their Prime Minister? Are they voted

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:42.810
for by the MPs as they do in European countries?
Or do they hold presidential elections like

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:50.120
they do in USA? Well, it’s actually nothing
like either of those… As I said, Kuwait

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:56.100
is a semi-democracy. This means the Head of
the State is the EMIR and he chooses the prime

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:57.710
minister and his cabinet.

00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:02.389
Does it sound sort of like those European
absolute monarchies that you studied at the

00:06:02.389 --> 00:06:07.240
history lessons? Well, it’s not exactly
like that... In fact, in Arab Monarchies,

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:11.880
the position of the Emir is not inherited.
This is why in Saudi Arabia they have big

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:16.880
internal battles to choose their leaders.
And, as I explained in a previous video, Royal

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:24.380
Families in this part of the planet can have
thousands of members.

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:28.759
So in the case of Kuwait, the members of their
Royal family, the so-called, AL-SABAH house

00:06:28.759 --> 00:06:34.229
can vote for the Emir. But right after, the
national assembly has to vote on whether they

00:06:34.229 --> 00:06:36.639
accept this decision or not.

00:06:36.639 --> 00:06:41.180
But wait just a minute because just incase
the system were not complicated enough, here

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:47.300
is another extra fact: the Constitution allows
the Emir to dissolve the parliament anytime

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:52.580
he wants. And, well, that’s something he
does pretty often…

00:06:52.580 --> 00:06:58.889
Emir of Kuwait dissolves parliament
The move, announced on state media after an

00:06:58.889 --> 00:07:02.440
emergency government meeting, sets the stage
for early elections.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:07.440
And, believe me, parliamentary debates in
Kuwait are far from being quiet. Emergency

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:11.680
meetings are a common thing and sometimes
its really hard to get to any kind of consensus.

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:17.300
For some analysts, this is one of the reasons
that explains this...

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:20.990
A CRUDE-A-HOLIC ECONOMY

00:07:20.990 --> 00:07:26.039
We all know it: oil-rich countries have so
much money they can spend it as if there was

00:07:26.039 --> 00:07:31.100
no tomorrow. Most natural-born Kuwaiti citizens
work as civil servants for the government.

00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:37.120
They pay no income tax, their energy bills
are subsidized, and their salaries are ludicrously

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:38.120
high.

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:44.960
The ones who work on the oil rigs are the
foreigners. But this is not only a reality

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:50.110
for Kuwait. It happens all over the region.
Black gold has allowed all of these countries

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:57.090
to have this way of life.

00:07:57.090 --> 00:08:03.940
But what happens now? As you know, the market
price for crude oil has fallen in recent years.

00:08:03.940 --> 00:08:08.330
Of course, these oil-monarchies are still
making profits, but not enough to keep that

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:13.759
system going. And this is why today, all of
these countries have fiscal deficits. This

00:08:13.759 --> 00:08:20.039
means their spending is way higher than their
income.

00:08:20.039 --> 00:08:27.759
Pay attention to the chart here! Even in USA,
where they are really worried about their

00:08:27.759 --> 00:08:33.479
high deficit, is doing better than this countries.
And now you might wonder... What does this

00:08:33.479 --> 00:08:38.160
figure actually mean? Well… this means that
if the Kuwaitis don’t want to go bankrupt

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:43.539
in a few years, they’d better find other
alternative incomes and not rely entirely

00:08:43.539 --> 00:08:44.539
on oil.

00:08:44.539 --> 00:08:48.570
Nonetheless, despite Kuwait having the most
modern and democratic political system, they

00:08:48.570 --> 00:08:58.610
have the highest dependence on crude oil.
Even Saudi Arabia, regressive as they are,

00:08:58.610 --> 00:09:02.970
is better prepared for a price in the price
of oil. And this is a surprise for everybody

00:09:02.970 --> 00:09:08.300
because, during the 1970s, Kuwait was the
rock star of the region. Now, this title goes

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:12.860
to Dubai, despite it being an absolute monarchy.
And this has left many Arabs wondering whether

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:22.960
democracy is compatible with economic reform.
Kuwait has stagnated, frustrating the people

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:25.980
of a country once seen as a Middle East trailblazer.

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:30.510
Let’s say you want to start a logistics
company in Dubai. You just need to buy some

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:35.981
land and build the facilities, right? Well,
in Kuwait, this is almost impossible. The

00:09:35.981 --> 00:09:41.160
government owns 90% of the territory. On the
other hand, bureaucracy has reached insane

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:45.269
levels. According to the World Bank, it´s
easier to start a business in countries like

00:09:45.269 --> 00:09:55.070
Ukraine or El Salvador than it is in Kuwait.
And all of this, despite the fact that Kuwait

00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:59.950
has a lower corporate tax than Luxembourg.
Added to this are the sky-high salaries of

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:04.790
civil workers, which rise year after year,
and you can probably imagine that no one is

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:09.350
going to become an entrepreneur and leave
behind the comfort and the safety of a government

00:10:09.350 --> 00:10:20.510
job.
But now, all of a sudden, the Qatari crisis

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:24.970
has offered Kuwait a chance to emerge as a
regional leader. Their royal house has good

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:30.660
relationships with all the countries involved:
including United States, Saudi Arabia and

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:36.890
Qatar. Plus, their political system is the
most open and democratic in the region. In

00:10:36.890 --> 00:10:42.040
other words, they have the best chance of
becoming a mediator in this crisis. And they

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:48.769
are well aware of it.
Kuwaiti Emir to travel to Saudi for Qatar

00:10:48.769 --> 00:10:49.769
talks

00:10:49.769 --> 00:10:54.760
So now the question is… Do you think Kuwait
can take back its role as a regional leader?

00:10:54.760 --> 00:10:59.120
Can this crisis help them to showcase their
country for foreign investment? Let us know

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:03.459
what you think in the comments below.

